Give RELION's ALTCPU CTIC/CTOC macros a thread-safe body, so the E-step's stage split is observable.

Applies on top of relion5-tt.patch (it needs src/acc/tt/ to exist). One file changes. Accumulation is
always compiled in; TT_RELION_PROFILE=1 gates the report, so the same binary serves a timed arm and a
profiled arm. See src_acc_tt/tt_profile.h for why neither RELION's -DTIMING timers nor its own CTIC
macros can produce this number.

diff --git a/src/acc/cpu/cpu_benchmark_utils.h b/src/acc/cpu/cpu_benchmark_utils.h
index a8daa31..baab47b 100644
--- a/src/acc/cpu/cpu_benchmark_utils.h
+++ b/src/acc/cpu/cpu_benchmark_utils.h
@@ -2,10 +2,11 @@
 #ifndef CPU_BENCHMARK_UTILS_H_
 #define CPU_BENCHMARK_UTILS_H_
 
-#define	CTIC(timer,timing)
-#define	CTOC(timer,timing)  
+#include "src/acc/tt/tt_profile.h"
+#define	CTIC(timer,timing) (TTProf::tic(timing))
+#define	CTOC(timer,timing) (TTProf::toc(timing))
 #define	GTIC(timer,timing)
-#define	GTOC(timer,timing) 
+#define	GTOC(timer,timing)
 #define	GATHERGPUTIMINGS(timer) 
 
 namespace CpuKernels
